    "working_thesis": "The modern age is defined by three foundational events—world alienation, the discovery of the Archimedean point in science, and the rise of Cartesian doubt—which together produced a profound reversal of the traditional hierarchical order between the vita contemplativa and the vita activa, culminating ultimately in the victory of the animal laborans and the triumph of life as the highest good."
